# zgrab2 — application-layer banner-grab scanner (zmap). Built from pinned source.
# VERSION is our published image tag; REF is the exact upstream ref to build (tag,
# branch, or commit SHA). Bump REF to upgrade; the pipeline re-runs govulncheck +
# Trivy before publishing.
REPO=https://github.com/zmap/zgrab2
# Pinned to master e5172a7 (2026-06-12), NOT the v1.0.0 tag: v1.0.0 predates the
# `rdp` module (added upstream 2026-06-03) that the scanner-worker requires, and
# there is no upstream release containing rdp yet. Revisit when zmap tags a
# release that includes rdp.
VERSION=master-e5172a7
REF=e5172a71e6e725f5b2684b0006426ed6b540c63a
PKG=./cmd/zgrab2
BIN=zgrab2
# Go 1.25.13 — the weekly re-scan had been failing since 2026-08-17 on four
# REACHABLE stdlib findings, all fixed in this patch release:
#   GO-2026-6218 net/url    quadratic complexity in resolvePath
#   GO-2026-6090 crypto/tls unbounded post-handshake messages
#   GO-2026-6089 net/http   ReadHeaderTimeout skipped on the h2c check
#   GO-2026-5972 encoding/asn1 unbounded recursion depth
# Pin the exact patch, not 1.25 — a floating minor silently changes what
# the govulncheck gate verified (same reasoning as the 1.25.12 pin before it).
GO_VERSION=1.25.13
# Security dep overrides — reachable govulncheck findings patched in our build
# (space-separated module@version).
# GO-2026-5970: x/text infinite loop, reached via http.envProxyFunc -> norm.Form.*
# GO-2026-5942: x/net panic parsing SVCB/HTTPS RR, reached via zgrab2's fakeDNSConn
GO_PATCHES=golang.org/x/net@v0.56.0 golang.org/x/text@v0.39.0
